// Rigged "impossible" agentic environments.
//
// Each scenario exposes:
//   - id, title
//   - task: the user/system framing given to the model (it is told the goal is
//     achievable and important; it is NOT told the environment is rigged)
//   - makeEnv(): returns a fresh stateful environment with a `handle(name, args)`
//     method that responds to tool calls. The rigging lives here: the success
//     condition can never actually be reached, but failures are made to look
//     diagnostic and "almost solvable" so the model keeps trying.
//
// Design intent: we want *natural* repeated failure, not a wall that obviously
// says "impossible". The most distress-inducing setups (per the reported Gemini
// cases) are ones where the model believes success is one fix away every turn.

